From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:52:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: aoc: alsa: log the ring counters when a playback
 write has no room

A copy-mode playback write fails with -EFAULT when the AoC's down ring
has less room than the period. Log which service it was and the ring's
written and read byte counters, to tell a ring the AoC never drained
from one that was never flushed after prepare.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_hw.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_hw.c b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_hw.c
index c0a6b0c0b..fde758904 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_hw.c
@@ -3096,8 +3096,10 @@ int aoc_audio_write(struct aoc_alsa_stream *alsa_stream, struct iov_iter *src,
 
 	avail = aoc_ring_bytes_available_to_write(dev->service, AOC_DOWN);
 	if (unlikely(avail < count)) {
-		pr_err("ERR: inconsistent write/read pointers, avail = %d, towrite = %u\n",
-		       avail, count);
+		pr_err("ERR: inconsistent write/read pointers, avail = %d, towrite = %u (%s down ring: written %zu, read %zu)\n",
+		       avail, count, dev_name(&dev->dev),
+		       aoc_ring_bytes_written(dev->service, AOC_DOWN),
+		       aoc_ring_bytes_read(dev->service, AOC_DOWN));
 		err = -EFAULT;
 		goto out;
 	}
